KO-04-C1  Commit-point crash matrix
A = 64B of 0x41 ('A'), B = 64B of 0x42 ('B'), document 'doc', real local file system, temp directories only

== Why: rename(2) of CURRENT is the single commit point
   put(B) never touches v1. It writes B to a NEW file v000002.dat (copy-on-write),
   fsyncs it, then writes a one-line pointer to a temp file .CURRENT.<pid>.tmp,
   fsyncs it and rename()s it over CURRENT (MoveFileEx REPLACE|WRITE_THROUGH on
   Windows). rename replaces the directory entry atomically: any observer sees
   the old CURRENT or the new one, never a mix. So:
     dies BEFORE the rename -> CURRENT still names v1 -> A; recovery deletes the
                               orphan v2 + temp (rolled back)
     dies AFTER the rename  -> CURRENT names v2 -> B; recovery verifies v2's
                               SHA-256, keeps it, flushes the directory (rolled forward)
   Recovery's rule: truth = CURRENT if it parses and its target verifies. The
   journal (BEGIN without COMMIT) only says WHICH saves were in flight.

